Please have a look at the code below.  In order to achieve the exact same behavior on both platforms, I need to invert the shouldShowRationale handling logic. I don't feel this is right, and requires platform-specific branches, which is exactly what a KMP library should solve IMHO.  This happens with any kind of permission (at least Camera and Location, that I've tried). I didn't choose Camera for any particular reason.  Please let me know if I am misusing the library.  Thanks for your work and time.

```
val cameraPermissionState = rememberPermissionState(Permission.Camera)
val isGranted = cameraPermissionState.status.isGranted
val shouldShowRationale = cameraPermissionState.status.shouldShowRationale

// ...

if (isGranted) {
    // Great ...
} else {
    if (isAndroid) {
        if (shouldShowRationale) {
            cameraPermissionState.openAppSettings()
        } else {
            cameraPermissionState.launchPermissionRequest()
        }
    } else if (isIos) {
        if (shouldShowRationale) {
            cameraPermissionState.launchPermissionRequest()
        } else {
            cameraPermissionState.openAppSettings()
        }
    }
}
```

